================== RUN: edge_exponent_check.py ==================
Soft-edge exponent of the ENERGY DOS rho(E), where rho(E) = mu(theta)*|dtheta/dE|.
Expect rho(E) ~ (E0-|E|)^s with s=1/2 (Wigner sqrt edge), independent of q.

       q | s_theta(mu vs phi) | s_E (rho vs edge-dist)
    0.30 |             2.0000 |                 0.5000
    0.50 |             2.0000 |                 0.5000
    0.70 |             2.0000 |                 0.5000
    0.90 |             2.0004 |                 0.5002
    0.95 |             2.0018 |                 0.5009
    0.99 |             2.0456 |                 0.5228

CONCLUSION: in THETA, mu ~ phi^2 (s_theta=2). In ENERGY, rho(E) ~ sqrt(E0-|E|) (s_E=1/2),
the universal Wigner sqrt soft edge -- q-independent. So the EDGE freezing exponent is
p_MOND=(s_E+1)/(s_E+2)=(1.5)/(2.5)=3/5 -> g~g_bar^0.6 = anti-MOND, for ANY q. The earlier
fixed-fraction window overstated s because it sat OUTSIDE the asymptotic sqrt regime.
The CENTER (rho ~ const, s_E=0 -> p=1/2 -> MOND) and EDGE (s_E=1/2 -> p=3/5 -> anti-MOND)
discriminator is therefore SOLID and q-robust. Only the PLACEMENT of |vac> is contested.

================== RUN: chord_vacuum_placement_test.py ==================
############################################################################################
# CLOSURE TEST: is theta_vac DERIVED by the chord algebra or an external dictionary?
############################################################################################

[TEST A] CHORD VACUUM |0>: <theta|0>^2 mu(theta) -- where does the algebra's own ground
         state of N_hat live? (q=0.7)
    peak at theta=1.5708 (pi/2=1.5708); mean|E|/E0=0.2215; frac within 5% of center=0.139
    => the chord vacuum |0> (N_hat ground state) sits at the spectral CENTER. [N-V-favorable]

[TEST C] HAMILTONIAN H=(a+a^dag)/sqrt(1-q): its eigenvalue E(theta)=2cos(theta)/sqrt(1-q).
    lowest E (H-ground)  at theta=pi  -> EDGE  (E=-E0=-3.651)
    highest E            at theta=0   -> EDGE  (E=+E0=3.651)
    E=0 / max entropy    at theta=pi/2-> CENTER
    => the algebra supplies BOTH a natural CENTER state (N_hat-vacuum / infinite-T /
       max-entropy) AND natural EDGE states (H extremal eigenstates).

[TEST B] THE EQUALS SIGN. de Sitter static patch = WHICH state?
    N-V 2310.16994 : |dS> := infinite-temperature (rho ~ Identity, max entropy) -> CENTER theta=pi/2
    Okuyama 2505.08116 : |dS> := triple-scaling saddle around theta=pi -> EDGE
    Both are states in the SAME chord Hilbert space; the chord commutation relations
    [a, a^dag]_q = 1 do NOT contain the clause 'static patch = center' or '= edge'.
    That identification is the HOLOGRAPHIC DICTIONARY, supplied externally.

